From 23f848e3499890524e648b3923d05ab6787f30ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bowehan <bowehan@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 12 Aug 2025 10:53:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] FROMLIST: drm/msm/dp: drop the entire HPD state machine

Since internal HPD IRQ event handling has been moved to being handled by the DRM framework detect() and hpd_notify() callbacks, there is no need for the MSM driver to track the HPD state separately.

Drop all references to the HPD state machine and replace existing checks
with checks for link_ready or sink_count.

Signed-off-by: Jessica Zhang <jessica.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: bowehan <bowehan@qti.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20250808-hpd-refactor-v2-11-7f4e1e741aa3@oss.qualcomm.com/
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/all/20250808-hpd-refactor-v2-11-7f4e1e741aa3@oss.qualcomm.com/]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 172 ++++++++--------------------
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+), 125 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 0a13e12ce2d0..d9b6561dcd1d 100644
